        "original_id": "ea6cdf1a-1d33-5254-8f53-963c6e1f06a6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Manhattan, New York City, Times Square, West 45th Street, Central Park\n- Buildings: Bertelsmann Building, 1540 Broadway, 432 Park Avenue, Loew's State Theatre\n\nFacts:\n- In 2011, 432 Park Avenue was originally proposed to be 1,300 feet tall.\n- 432 Park Avenue later topped out at 1,396 feet.\n- The former Bertelsmann Building is now known as 1540 Broadway.\n- 1540 Broadway is a 44-story, 733-foot office tower in Times Square in Manhattan, New York City, on West 45th Street.\n- 432 Park Avenue is a residential skyscraper in New York City that overlooks Central Park.\n- Loew's State Theatre closed on February 19, 1987.\n- The site of Loew's State Theatre is now occupied by the Bertelsmann Building.",
